<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ethan Allen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1738">1738</a>–<a href="/years/1789">1789</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ethan Allen was an American frontiersman, land speculator and revolutionary leader, a founder of Vermont. As leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/green-mountain-boys">Green Mountain Boys</a> he resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>'s claims to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire-grants">New Hampshire Grants</a> and in 1775 captured Fort Ticonderoga. Captured by the British in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> later that year, he was a prisoner until 1778. With his brothers he later held secret talks with British Canada about Vermont's future.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ethan-allen.jpg" alt="Ethan Allen" width="320" height="749" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USCapitol · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_-_USCapitol_-_Ethan_Allen_Statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
